<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  This file exists for exactly one key.

	  Everything else in Bleat's Info.plist is generated: the target sets
	  GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE and a handful of INFOPLIST_KEY_* build settings,
	  which is the house style and means there is no plist to drift. But there
	  is no INFOPLIST_KEY_ for CFBundleURLTypes — the generated set covers a
	  fixed list of keys and URL types is not on it — so registering a scheme
	  needs a real file. Xcode merges the generated keys *into* this one when
	  both settings are present, so the camera usage string and the rest are
	  still build settings and still live in the project; only what cannot be
	  expressed there is written out here.

	  The scheme string must match PairingPayload.urlScheme in BleatKit, which
	  is what `bleat pair` puts in the QR. There is no way to assert that from
	  a package test — this file belongs to the app target — so it is stated in
	  both places and in CLAUDE.md.
	-->
	<!--
	  Local networking. Both keys are here rather than as INFOPLIST_KEY_ build
	  settings: NSBonjourServices is an array, which the generated set cannot
	  express, and separating the pair would leave the purpose string far from
	  the service it explains.

	  Herdr runs on a Mac on the same network, reached over SSH at a `.local`
	  name or a LAN address — both of which iOS gates behind the local network
	  permission. Without the usage description the system alert carries no
	  explanation of why a terminal client wants the network; without the
	  Bonjour service declaration, NWBrowser cannot ask the question at all,
	  which is how the app finds out whether permission was granted.
	-->
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Bleat connects over SSH to the Mac running Herdr. On your own network that Mac is a .local name or a local address, which iOS treats as a local network connection.</string>
	<key>NSBonjourServices</key>
	<array>
		<string>_ssh._tcp</string>
	</array>
	<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
			<string>Viewer</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLName</key>
			<string>dev.herdr.bleat.pairing</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
			<array>
				<string>bleat</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
